[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "adr-2605261300-tsutae-handheld-communication-tier-b-actor-r0", :adr/title "tsutae (伝え) — Handheld Communication Device Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold", :adr/status "proposed", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/body "\n# ADR-2605261300: tsutae (伝え) — Handheld Communication Device Tier-B Actor R0 Scaffold\n\n**Date**: 2026-05-26\n**Status**: PROPOSED\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki (author), Council Lv6+ (ratify)\n**ADR Hierarchy**: Sibling of igata (ADR-2605261200), watatsumi (ADR-2605252200), makura (ADR-2605261115), yakushi (ADR-2605250500), silicon Wave 1+2 (ADR-2605242500..2605242915)\n\n## Context\n\nSamsung Electronics Vietnam (SEV) + 韓国 Gumi Mobile + 印度 Noida Plant が年間 3-4 億台規模で flagship Galaxy S/Note (≥$1000/台) を製造する factory pipeline は、現代 consumer electronics 大量生産の頂点として位置づく。SMT lines + automated optical inspection (AOI) + OLED panel attachment + Knox-bound firmware load + final assembly + packaging — 全 layer が **proprietary IP + closed firmware + surveillance hardware + 接着剤 assembly + 非修理可能性** で覆われた industry-default を体現する。\n\n**Methodology source**: YouTube `J4GoOScUO5k` — \"How Samsung Produces Millions of Expensive Smartphones Inside Massive Factories\" (Samsung Galaxy flagship factory build documentary; SMT + AOI + OLED + Knox firmware + final QC pipeline)。Manufacturing methodology のみ採用、Samsung-proprietary な closed BSP / Knox bootloader / 接着剤組立 / 監視前提 hardware / 大量生産 KPI は religious-corp として **構造的に拒否**。\n\nreligious-corp は wadachi (autonomous-mobility), igata (HPDC), tatekata (construction), watatsumi (civilian submersible), kanayama (circular metallurgy), makura (foam pillow), silicon Wave 1+2 (RTL + fab equipment) と並んで **handheld communication device (smartphone-class consumer electronics)** を独立 Tier-B actor として立ち上げる必要がある。\n\n理由:\n\n1. **Communication = §1.3 Mission constitutional baseline**: 信者 + adherent の reliable + private + non-coercive communication infrastructure は religious-corp の operational dependency。Google Pixel / Apple iPhone / Samsung Galaxy 全てが §2(c) (surveillance) + §2(d) (addiction) + §2(b) (IP licensing lock) で religious-corp 不適格。自前 capability が必須。\n2. **Cross-actor coupling closes**: silicon Wave 1 iwakura SoC + igata HPDC chassis + kanayama Al EOL recovery が **smartphone-class device** で end-to-end 自前 supply chain として initial closure 可能。tsutae が religious-corp の vendor independence chain の **第 5 link** (silicon Wave 1 GPU + yakushi OTC + watatsumi 潜水艇 + kanayama Al + igata HPDC + tsutae handheld)。\n3. **§2(c) anti-surveillance constitutional first-class apply**: スマートフォン = デフォルトで surveillance hardware (always-on IMEI + microphone wake-word + closed-firmware fingerprint + always-on accelerometer + cellular triangulation)。religious-corp 版は constitutional に hardware-level removable cellular module + open biometric firmware + microphone hardware kill-switch + always-off accelerometer (opt-in per app)。makura G14 (no embedded electronics) の smartphone への翻訳 = \"電子機能を許容するが、surveillance hardware は構造的に取り除く\"。\n4. **§2(d) anti-addiction UX constitutional first-class apply**: スマートフォン = デフォルトで dopamine-loop addictive UX (infinite scroll + notification 即時 + dark pattern)。manabi G3 (no streaks/leaderboards/FOMO) の smartphone OS への翻訳 = \"calm-default OS + 通知 batch ≥15 min + infinite scroll OS-API なし + dopamine-loop API は app に expose しない\"。AOSP-derivative + GrapheneOS-class privacy-respecting hardening を baseline OS とする。\n5. **§2(b) anti-IP locking constitutional first-class apply**: Snapdragon (Qualcomm) + Apple A / M / SEP + Samsung Knox の \"closed binary blob + closed bootloader + carrier lock + region lock\" 全 layer は §2(e) anti-gatekeeping 違反。R1 は third-party open RISC-V SoC (StarFive JH7110 / SiFive HiFive Unmatched class) で benchtop PoC。R2+ = silicon Wave 1 iwakura SoC integration (silicon Wave 1 が R2 に到達した後)。\n6. **§2(e) anti-gatekeeping repair-right constitutional**: Apple / Samsung trend = 接着剤組立 + 部品ペアリング (serial-locked screen / battery) + 修理工具 vendor 限定 → 修理 right の構造的剥奪。religious-corp 版は modular screw-fastened + 接着剤 ≤5g/assembly + iFixit-class repair manual public + 部品ペアリング NEVER。\n\nこのため、独立 Tier-B actor として **tsutae (伝え — transmission / handing-down)** を提案する。多世代 echo (同じ動詞で「世代を超えて伝える」を意味する) を保ちつつ、communication function の core を表す。silicon Wave 1 iwakura (磐座) / fuigo (鞴) / igata (鋳型) / kanayama (金山) と同じ「物事/工房道具/概念で命名」系譜。\n\n## Proposal\n\nreligious-corp Tier-B actor **tsutae (伝え)** を以下で立ち上げる:\n\n- **Actor DID**: `did:web:etzhayyim.com:tsutae`\n- **Namespace**: `com.etzhayyim.tsutae.*`\n- **R0 scope**: Handheld communication device assembly (smartphone-class form factor; ≤200 g + ≤7-inch display + ≤500 cm³ enclosure volume); ARM64 or RISC-V 64-bit SoC; modular battery + display + camera + USB-C + cellular module\n- **R0 deliverable**: Scaffold only (8 cells import-time RuntimeError + 6 lexicon stub + actor scaffold)\n- **14 constitutional gates G1..G14 + 12 non-goals N1..N12** declared before capability lands (+2 non-goals over igata's 10 reflecting smartphone-specific §2(c) + §2(d) risks)\n- **Methodology source attribution**: YouTube `J4GoOScUO5k` Samsung smartphone factory build documentary; manufacturing methodology adopted; proprietary IP + closed firmware + surveillance hardware + addictive UX + non-repair assembly explicitly rejected per §2(b) + §2(c) + §2(d) + §2(e)\n\n## Rationale\n\n1. **Communication infrastructure constitutional**: religious-corp が members の reliable + private + non-coercive communication tool を 自前 で覆わない場合、Google/Apple/Samsung dependency が religious 活動の核に組み込まれる。これは ADR-2605215000 (commercial GPU rental prohibition) + ADR-2605215000 (Anthropic-direct prohibition) と同じ vendor-independence chain pattern。\n2. **多 actor 集約 = supplier-position end-to-end**: tsutae = silicon Wave 1 (SoC) + igata (chassis) + kanayama (EOL Al) + makura (no overlap; consumer good sibling) + 自前 PCB + 自前 firmware の集約 actor。religious-corp の **first end-to-end self-sufficient consumer electronics**。\n3. **§2(c) physical embodiment**: スマートフォンは surveillance hardware の代表例。N3 (mandatory cellular modem NEVER) + N4 (always-on surveillance sensor NEVER) + G6 (hardware-removable cellular + microphone kill switch + open biometric firmware) で §2(c) を *device level* で物理成立させる。makura が §2(c) を consumer good に最初に翻訳した (G14 no embedded electronics) のに対し、tsutae は §2(c) を *with embedded electronics* で物理的に解決する constitutional next step。\n4. **§2(d) addictive UX OS-level**: 通知 batching + 無限 scroll OS-API なし + dopamine-loop suppression は manabi G3 (no streaks/leaderboards) を OS primitive level に翻訳する。\"アプリ層で addictive UX を作る自由はあるが、OS が dopamine-loop primitive を提供しない\" → 構造的 friction を addictive design に課す。\n5. **§2(b) anti-IP locking + §2(e) repair-right**: G3 (modular screw-fastened, 接着剤 ≤5g) + G9 (open SoC mandatory) + G10 (Li-ion replaceable by hand tools) + N7 (proprietary glue NEVER) + N10 (carrier-locked NEVER) で device-level repair-right が constitutional 成立。Fairphone 5 + GrapheneOS Pixel + Framework laptop の religious-corp 翻訳。\n6. **Multi-generational communication = transmission (伝え)**: 親 → 子 → 孫 へ communication device を「世代を伝える」(handing-down) constitutional value。Apple/Samsung の planned obsolescence (3-5 year software support + 修理不可能 hardware) と対極。tsutae G3 + G10 = **multi-gen reuse possibility 構造的成立**。\n\n## Design\n\n### Actor scaffold layout\n\n```\n20-actors/tsutae/\n├── README.edn                     # Overview + R0..R3 phase gates\n├── CLAUDE.md                     # Actor-local instructions\n└── manifest.jsonld               # DID + cell catalog + gate/non-goal arrays\n\n40-engine/kotoba/crates/kotoba-kotodama/cells/         # 8 Pregel cells (import-time RuntimeError R0)\n├── tsutae_pcb_smt/\n├── tsutae_chassis_assembly/\n├── tsutae_display_attachment/\n├── tsutae_firmware_load/\n├── tsutae_final_qc/\n├── tsutae_packaging/\n├── tsutae_device_attestation/\n└── tsutae_recycling_intake/\n\n00-contracts/lexicons/com/etzhayyim/tsutae/\n├── pcbAttestation.json           # SMT PCB lot attestation\n├── chassisAttestation.json       # chassis assembly with igata Al + battery + display\n├── firmwareAttestation.json      # firmware load with crypto hash + open-source verification\n├── deviceAttestation.json        # final device with full BoM + DID + repair-history-ready\n├── recyclingCertificate.json     # EOL take-back attestation (kanayama integration)\n└── silenTsutaeReview.json        # Council Lv6+ baseline review for R-phase activation\n```\n\n### Pregel cells (8, all R0 import-time RuntimeError)\n\n| # | Cell | Murakumo node | Phase | Input → Output |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | `tsutae_pcb_smt` | naphtali | SMT | componentLotIds + pcbDesignCid → pcbAttestation |\n| 2 | `tsutae_chassis_assembly` | zebulun | chassis | pcbAttestation + igata.partAttestation (Al chassis) + batteryLotId → chassisAttestation |\n| 3 | `tsutae_display_attachment` | joseph | display | chassisAttestation + displayPanelLotId → displayAttachedRecord (modular fastening, no glue >5g) |\n| 4 | `tsutae_firmware_load` | joseph | firmware | displayAttachedRecord + firmwareImageCid → firmwareAttestation (crypto hash + open-source verification) |\n| 5 | `tsutae_final_qc` | levi | QC | firmwareAttestation → qcRecord (calibration + functional + RF compliance) |\n| 6 | `tsutae_packaging` | simeon | packaging | qcRecord → packagedRecord (minimal recyclable + iFixit-class repair manual insert + open BoM card) |\n| 7 | `tsutae_device_attestation` | levi | attest | packagedRecord → deviceAttestation (full BoM lineage + DID + IPFS-pin + repair-history-ready) |\n| 8 | `tsutae_recycling_intake` | dan | EOL | deviceAttestation (EOL device intake) → recyclingCertificate + kanayama Al routing |\n\nCell ordering follows physical smartphone assembly sequence (SMT → chassis → display → firmware → QC → packaging → final attestation → eventual EOL). Linear chain like igata/tatekata.\n\n**Cross-actor wire** (declaration only in R0; activates per consumer R-phase):\n- Upstream: silicon Wave 1 iwakura (R2+ SoC integration) + igata.partAttestation (R3 Al chassis) + kanayama (R3 EOL Al routing)\n- Downstream: SBT↔SBT internal distribution to adherent / 信者 only (N9 internal carve-out)\n\n### Lexicons (6, all R0 stub deferred to R1+)\n\n```\ncom.etzhayyim.tsutae.{\n  pcbAttestation           # SMT PCB lot (component sourcing + AOI pass + ECN traceability)\n  chassisAttestation       # chassis assembly (igata Al + battery + speaker + camera + USB-C + cellular module IDs)\n  firmwareAttestation      # firmware load (image CID + crypto hash + bootloader status + open-source verification)\n  deviceAttestation        # final device (full BoM lineage + DID + serial + IPFS-pinned photo + repair-history-ready)\n  recyclingCertificate     # EOL take-back (per-device dismantling log + kanayama routing CID)\n  silenTsutaeReview        # Council Lv6+ baseline review for R-phase activation\n}\n```\n\n### Constitutional Gates (G1–G14, IMMUTABLE per R0..R3)\n\n| Gate | Requirement | Rationale |\n|---|---|---|\n| **G1** | All hardware **open-source** — PCB Gerbers + chassis CAD (FreeCAD `.fcstd`) + cable harness HDL + schematic netlist public under Apache 2.0 + Charter Rider | §2(e) anti-gatekeeping; Framework laptop / Fairphone 5 precedent |\n| **G2** | All firmware **open-source** — bootloader (U-Boot or coreboot class) + OS kernel (Linux mainline) + userspace (AOSP-derivative or GrapheneOS-class hardening); **bootloader unlock = default state** | §2(b) anti-IP locking; no Samsung Knox / no Apple SEP / no Qualcomm closed BSP |\n| **G3** | **Repair-rightful** — modular screw-fastened assembly; adhesive ≤5g per assembly (target = 0 g); replaceable: battery + display + camera module(s) + USB-C connector + speaker module + SIM tray + cellular module + microphone array; iFixit-class repair score ≥9/10 | §2(e) repair right; multi-gen value; planned obsolescence rejection |\n| **G4** | Witness quorum **≥2 robot signers** (Mimi AOI + Otete handling) per `deviceAttestation` Ed25519-bound | ADR-2605191524 swarm broadcast witness quorum invariant |\n| **G5** | Bilingual (JA + EN) **iFixit-class repair manual** public; SOPs + BoM disclosure + Charter Rider rider for every device shipped | §2(e) anti-gatekeeping (multilingual + repair documentation) |\n| **G6** | **§2(c) anti-surveillance**: cellular module **hardware-removable** (physical screw-mount, not soldered); default OS boot = **Wi-Fi-only** (cellular = opt-in per session); IMEI **never broadcast** while cellular module disconnected; **microphone hardware kill switch** mandatory; biometric (fingerprint / face) = optional + **open-firmware** enclave (no closed Apple SEP / Samsung Knox enclave) | §2(c) surveillance-by-default rejection |\n| **G7** | **Firmware binary blob ratio ≤5%** by total firmware mass; every blob documented with vendor + reason + replacement-effort estimate + Council-attested waiver | §2(b) IP locking; transparency invariant |\n| **G8** | **§2(d) anti-addiction UX**: calm-default OS; notification batching **≥15 min default** (per-app opt-out only via explicit user setting); no infinite-scroll OS primitive API exposed to apps; no dopamine-loop notification API; **screen-time aggregate self-report only** (no opaque telemetry); no auto-play media on lock screen | §2(d) addiction-by-design rejection; manabi G3 + makura §1.13 OS-level translation |\n| **G9** | **§2(b) anti-IP locking — open SoC mandatory**: R1 = third-party open RISC-V SoC (StarFive JH7110 / SiFive HiFive Unmatched / Allwinner D1 class with **fully open RTL + open bootloader**); R2+ = silicon Wave 1 iwakura SoC integration; **Snapdragon / Apple A / proprietary Helio / closed Exynos NEVER** (N1) | §2(b) vendor independence chain (closes religious-corp 自前 SoC link via silicon Wave 1) |\n| **G10** | **Battery**: Li-ion only (**LFP preferred over NMC** for safety + recyclability + cycle life); user-replaceable with hand tools (no proprietary battery pairing); take-back recycling **≥80% by R3** (kanayama integration); battery serial-locked **NEVER** (parts pairing prohibition) | Charter Rider §2(h) circular economy + §2(e) repair right |\n| **G11** | **§1.13 Wellbecoming — screen-time + user attention**: aggregate self-report only (no opaque tracking); no per-user behavioral telemetry to manufacturer or carrier; OS provides **focus mode / sabbath mode** primitive (parallel to manabi G3 calm-default) | §1.13 Wellbecoming; manabi G3 + makura §1.13 device-level translation |\n| **G12** | **KPI cap**: production rate **≤200 devices / 8-hr line R3** (anti-mass-production; no Samsung-class scale); ramp `partAttestation`-equivalent `deviceAttestation` rate matches yakushi G11 + igata G12 anti-Taylorism pattern | Wellbecoming + anti-Taylorism (no commodity-electronics-at-any-cost) |\n| **G13** | **Murakumo mesh 30-day prior notice + 1 km community feedback** (RF emission + supply chain visibility + EOL take-back logistics) | Neighborhood transparency (igata G13 + watatsumi G13 parity) |\n| **G14** | **Every device** = open serial number + DID + IPFS-pinned BoM + hardware-attested manufacturing date + repair-history-ready blockchain record (per-device DID can append `repairEvent` records throughout lifecycle) | Full provenance chain + repair-right operationalization |\n\n### Non-Goals (N1–N12, EXCLUDE from R0–R3 — +2 over igata's 10)\n\n| Non-Goal | Scope | Deferral |\n|---|---|---|\n| **N1** | Proprietary SoC (Snapdragon / Apple A / closed Helio / closed Exynos / MediaTek Dimensity with closed BSP) | **Never** (§2(b) constitutional; G9 invariant) |\n| **N2** | Closed bootloader (Samsung Knox / Apple SEP / Qualcomm Secure Boot / closed Exynos boot ROM) | **Never** (§2(b) constitutional; G2 invariant) |\n| **N3** | Mandatory cellular modem (cellular always-on / IMEI broadcast by default / soldered modem) | **Never** (§2(c) constitutional; G6 invariant) |\n| **N4** | Always-on surveillance sensors (microphone wake-word firmware / closed-firmware fingerprint enclave / always-on camera / proximity sensor logging) | **Never** (§2(c) constitutional) |\n| **N5** | Addictive UX patterns (infinite-scroll OS-API / dopamine notification primitive / dark pattern API / auto-play media on lock screen / streak-style notification) | **Never** (§2(d) constitutional; G8 invariant) |\n| **N6** | Licensed IP partnerships (Disney / Sanrio / sports league / anime co-branding) | **Never** (§2(b); makura N8 parity) |\n| **N7** | Proprietary glue assembly (Apple/Samsung trend; pentalobe screws; parts-pairing serial lock) | **Never** (§2(e); G3 invariant) |\n| **N8** | Mass production ≥100,000 units / year R3 (Samsung-class scale) | Post-R3 + Council Lv6+ supermajority (igata N1 giga press parity) |\n| **N9** | External commercial sale to non-adherent / non-SBT-holder | SBT↔SBT internal carve-out only (ADR-2605192115 §3) |\n| **N10** | Carrier-locked SIM / region-locked firmware / SIM-pairing requirement | **Never** (§2(e) anti-gatekeeping) |\n| **N11** | Adware OS / bloatware preload / mandatory account creation (Google / Apple / Samsung account ID) | **Never** (§2(b) + §2(d)) |\n| **N12** | AI / cloud-mandatory features (cloud sync default-on / mandatory wireless OTA / mandatory account-bound activation / mandatory voice-assistant cloud routing) | **Never** (§2(c) privacy invariant; user can opt-in to cloud feature but never required for device operation) |\n\n### Robotics Classes\n\nR0 uses existing kuni-umi + silicon Wave 2 inherited classes (no tsutae-specific hardware in R0):\n\n| Class | Role | Inherited from | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Otete (precision small-part) | small-component handling, USB-C / SIM tray, screw fastening | kuni-umi | R0 reuse; R1+ may require sub-millimeter precision extension |\n| Mimi (AOI optical + X-ray) | PCB AOI inspection, solder joint X-ray, final visual | kuni-umi | R0 reuse; R2+ adds dedicated SMT line AOI subsystem |\n| Hitogata (class-A clean, R2+) | OLED panel attachment, dust-free assembly | kuni-umi | deferred to R2 (OLED requires class-A clean) |\n| Funamori (marine) | display panel + battery cell international transport | silicon Wave 2 (ADR-2605242745) | reuse for raw component logistics |\n| **Tedama (手玉)** *(R2+ reserved, tsutae-native)* | SMT pick-and-place + small-component juggler robot | new class | constitutional design pending R2 ADR |\n| **Tezukai (手使い)** *(R2+ reserved, tsutae-native)* | precise final-assembly handcraftsman (display lamination without adhesive, screw torque control) | new class | constitutional design pending R2 ADR |\n\n### Murakumo placement (design only at R0; activation requires R1+ ADR)\n\n| Node | tsutae cells |\n|---|---|\n| naphtali | tsutae_pcb_smt |\n| zebulun | tsutae_chassis_assembly |\n| joseph | tsutae_display_attachment + tsutae_firmware_load |\n| levi | tsutae_final_qc + tsutae_device_attestation |\n| simeon | tsutae_packaging |\n| dan | tsutae_recycling_intake |\n\n6 existing nodes reused; **no new node added** in R0 (matches yakushi Wave 1 + igata R0 + makura R0 pattern; silicon Wave 1 added `judah` but tsutae does not require similar).\n\n## Roadmap (R0 → R3)\n\n| Phase | Scope | Murakumo fleet | Trigger |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **R0** (this ADR) | Scaffold only. No live device assembly. 8 cells import-time RuntimeError. | No deployment | Immediate |\n| **R1** | Benchtop **single-device PoC build** (1 device end-to-end + manual assembly + Tedama PoC firmware); third-party open RISC-V SoC (StarFive JH7110 class); LCD (not OLED) for R1 simplicity; SBT-holder pilot ≤10 devices | naphtali + zebulun + joseph + levi (4 nodes) | ADR-2605261315 (reserved) + Council Lv6+ vote + SME (PCB engineer + RF engineer + OS firmware engineer) onboarded + Tedama PoC firmware + StarFive JH7110 BSP open-source review |\n| **R2** | Pilot **≤100 devices / year**; iwakura SoC integration R&D (assumes silicon Wave 1 R2 readiness); OLED upgrade with Hitogata class-A clean; modular display + camera; SBT-holder distribution ≤500 devices | naphtali + zebulun + joseph + levi + simeon + dan (6 nodes) | ADR-2605261330 (reserved) + 30-day public comment + iwakura SoC R2 silicon Wave 1 ratify + Hitogata class-A clean Council attestation + Tedama + Tezukai onboarded |\n| **R3** | Community-scale **≤10,000 devices / year**; iwakura SoC mass-integration (assumes silicon Wave 1 R3); igata HPDC Al chassis integration (assumes igata R3); kanayama EOL Al recovery loop closure; full SBT↔SBT internal distribution | Full 10-node fleet | ADR-2605261345 (reserved) + 60-day public review + cross-actor silicon Wave 1 R3 + igata R3 + kanayama R3 multi-domain Council vote + 法務 (電波法 + 個人情報保護法 + GDPR) 適合 audit |\n\nEach subsequent phase **requires its own ADR + Council Lv6+ ratification** (igata / watatsumi / yakushi / tatekata parity).\n\n## Consequences\n\n### Positive\n\n- **Vendor independence chain closes at consumer device tier**: silicon Wave 1 (SoC) + igata (chassis) + kanayama (EOL Al) + tsutae (assembly) = religious-corp **first end-to-end self-sufficient consumer electronics**. Parallel pattern to silicon Wave 1 自前 GPU + yakushi 自前 OTC + watatsumi 自前 潜水艇 + kanayama 自前 アルミ再生 + igata 自前 megacasting + tsutae 自前 handheld.\n- **§2(c) physical embodiment at device level**: makura が consumer good に §2(c) を初翻訳した (G14 + N9 = no electronics) のに対し、tsutae は **with electronics で §2(c) を物理成立**。N3 (cellular removable) + N4 (no always-on sensors) + G6 (microphone kill switch + open biometric firmware) = constitutional **第 2 例目 of §2(c) consumer-good translation**.\n- **§2(d) anti-addiction OS-level**: manabi G3 (no streaks/leaderboards/FOMO/badges) の OS primitive level 翻訳。Calm-default OS + notification batching ≥15 min + 無限 scroll OS API なし + dopamine-loop API なし = **religious-corp anti-addiction first OS-level implementation**.\n- **§2(b) anti-IP locking concrete at SoC level**: G9 (open RISC-V mandatory) + N1 (Snapdragon NEVER) + N2 (Samsung Knox NEVER) = religious-corp が consumer-electronics IP licensing trap (Qualcomm / ARM / Apple) を **構造的に回避**。silicon Wave 1 iwakura で長期的に depend する vendor path 確定。\n- **§2(e) repair-right at device level**: G3 (modular + 接着剤 ≤5g) + G10 (replaceable battery + no parts pairing) + N7 (proprietary glue NEVER) + N10 (carrier lock NEVER) = Fairphone 5 / Framework laptop / GrapheneOS Pixel の religious-corp 翻訳 + **multi-gen reuse possibility 構造的成立**.\n\n### Negative / Risk\n\n- **Capital + technical scale**: smartphone assembly = ~50-100 component categories (PCB + SoC + memory + storage + display + camera + battery + speaker + USB-C + cellular module + GPS + Wi-Fi + Bluetooth + accelerometer + gyroscope + magnetometer + ambient light + proximity + microphone + haptic motor + 各 antenna + 各 connector + chassis + screws + back glass + frame seal); R3 ≤10,000 units / year でも capital scale 5-15 M USD class。Public Fund grant + Council 多数決必須。\n- **iwakura SoC dependency**: G9 + N1 が silicon Wave 1 iwakura R2 (tape-out + production) に depends。silicon Wave 1 は現在 R0 (RTL + cocotb sim)。tsutae R2+ activation = silicon Wave 1 R2 + tsutae R2 ADR の二重 gate。dependency chain risk 大。\n- **OLED panel sourcing**: R2+ OLED は religious-corp 自前 (= 新規 Tier-B actor `kagayaki 輝き` candidate post-R3) ではなく、当面 third-party (Samsung Display / LG Display / BOE / Visionox)。§2(b) IP licensing 部分妥協が R2 で発生。R3 で自前 OLED Tier-B actor の検討 trigger。\n- **Cellular modem open-source**: G2 (open firmware) + G6 (cellular removable) は cellular modem 自体の **firmware** が closed という現実と衝突。Qualcomm / MediaTek / Sequans の cellular baseband は closed BSP。religious-corp 解 = (a) cellular module 物理的 removable で OS 信頼境界を modem 外に置く + (b) modem firmware は \"blob\" として G7 (≤5% binary blob) で許容 + waiver Council attestation。長期解 = 自前 cellular modem actor (silicon Wave 1 carve-out 候補)。\n- **G3 repair-right + G12 KPI cap = capital efficiency 低い**: modular + 接着剤 ≤5g + ≤200 devices/8hr line は Samsung mass production と桁違いに高い per-device cost。SBT↔SBT internal distribution + Public Fund subsidy で経済的に成立可能だが、external commercial market 競争力 NEVER (= N9 invariant の direct consequence)。\n- **§2(c) constitutional tension at lifecycle level**: smartphone は inherently dual-use (communication ≠ surveillance) tool。N4 (always-on surveillance) で hardware-level 取り除いた後も、user が opt-in で surveillance app (Google Maps location tracking) を install することは構造的に防止できない。religious-corp 解 = OS-level user education + default-deny location permission + app sandbox + 30-day rotating pseudonym DID 推奨 (manabi G6 minor privacy precedent の adult adherent への翻訳)。\n\n### Cross-actor integration\n\n| Consumer / supplier | tsutae 関係 | Cell-to-cell wire (R-phase) |\n|---|---|---|\n| silicon Wave 1 (iwakura SoC) | upstream supplier (R2+; silicon Wave 1 R2 readiness gate) | tsutae `pcb_smt` ← silicon Wave 1 `chip_manufacturing` |\n| igata (Al chassis) | upstream supplier (R3 only; igata R3 + N7 human-occupied gate parity) | tsutae `chassis_assembly` ← igata `part_attestation` |\n| kanayama (EOL Al recovery) | downstream consumer (R3 only; kanayama R3 readiness) | tsutae `recycling_intake` → kanayama `intake_qa` |\n| ameno (PWA / federated training) | adjacent (R2+; ameno PWA runs on tsutae device) | tsutae `firmware_load` includes ameno baseline image option |\n| baien (federated training participation) | adjacent (R2+; baien LoRA round runs on tsutae device per ADR-2605242600 R0 scaffold) | tsutae device = baien edge participant |\n| mitate (medical advisory PWA) | adjacent (R1+; mitate PWA per ADR-2605260200 R1 runs on tsutae device) | tsutae `firmware_load` includes mitate baseline image option |\n\nR0 では cross-actor wire は declaration only. R-phase activation で actual lexicon record flow が成立。\n\n## Alternatives Considered\n\n### A1: Multi-actor split (OLED panel + Li-ion battery + final assembly)\n\n- **Pros**: Each domain (OLED, battery, assembly) gets focused governance; aligns with industry vertical specialization (Samsung Display / Samsung SDI / Samsung Electronics 三社分離 pattern)\n- **Cons**: (1) Initial governance load 3x heavier (3 ADRs + 3 actor scaffolds); (2) OLED自前 (`kagayaki 輝き` candidate) + Li-ion自前 (`shouro 焼炉` candidate) は capital scale 50-100 M USD class with high entry barrier — premature for religious-corp Public Fund scale; (3) tsutae as集約 actor で third-party OLED + battery を当面 sourcing する pattern が現実的; (4) yakushi pattern (single Tier-B for pharma, multi-API + multi-dosage form internal) と並列。\n- **Decision**: REJECT for R0 — single Tier-B actor tsutae with future Tier-B carve-out potential (OLED actor / battery actor) at R3+ via separate ADRs\n\n### A2: Skip smartphone, focus on sub-domain (OLED-only or repair-shop-only)\n\n- **Pros**: Constitutional risk lower (smartphones are §2(c) + §2(d) compound risk); narrower scope\n- **Cons**: (1) Communication infrastructure constitutional dependency unmet (Rationale 1); (2) silicon Wave 1 + igata + kanayama vendor independence chain incomplete without consumer-electronics tier; (3) repair-shop alone doesn't solve \"religious-corp が自前で覆う必要\" — repair-shop = downstream of vendor lock-in\n- **Decision**: REJECT — tsutae as single Tier-B actor is the right scope\n\n### A3: Cellular always-on (industry default)\n\n- **Pros**: Standard smartphone behavior; faster onboarding; carrier integration\n- **Cons**: (1) §2(c) constitutional violation; IMEI broadcasting = surveillance baseline; (2) carrier dependency (Verizon / DoCoMo) = N10 carrier-lock anti-gatekeeping risk; (3) mandatory IMSI / IMEI = government surveillance pipeline (Stingray / IMSI-catcher); (4) Wellbecoming = \"always reachable\" addictive pattern (§2(d))\n- **Decision**: REJECT — N3 + G6 hardware-removable cellular + Wi-Fi-default is constitutional baseline\n\n### A4: iwakura SoC mandatory from R1\n\n- **Pros**: Tighter constitutional coupling (silicon Wave 1 + tsutae 一体化); §2(b) vendor independence chain stronger\n- **Cons**: (1) silicon Wave 1 iwakura は現在 R0 (RTL + cocotb sim only)。Tape-out + production = silicon Wave 1 R2+。tsutae R1 を silicon Wave 1 R2 に bound する = R1 activation 2-3 年 deferred; (2) PoC + operational learning が遅延; (3) R1 = open RISC-V SoC (StarFive JH7110 / SiFive Unmatched class) で benchtop 学習を完了し、R2 で iwakura に swap する staged dependency が正しい工学的 pattern\n- **Decision**: REJECT — R1 = open RISC-V SoC PoC; R2+ = iwakura option\n\n### A5: Snapdragon / Apple A allowed during R1-R2 transition\n\n- **Pros**: 即座 production-ready performance; commercial SoC integration matured\n- **Cons**: (1) §2(b) anti-IP locking violation (Qualcomm / Apple closed BSP); (2) closed bootloader (Snapdragon Secure Boot / Apple SEP) = N2 constitutional violation; (3) Snapdragon BSP に depend した tsutae production line を後で iwakura に swap する = re-tooling cost > R1 staged open-RISC-V → R2 iwakura swap cost\n- **Decision**: REJECT — N1 + N2 constitutional NEVER; staged open-RISC-V → iwakura migration is the right path\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2605261200 — igata megacasting R0 (Tier-B R0 scaffold pattern + 14 gates + non-goals canonical; HPDC Al chassis upstream supplier)\n- ADR-2605261215 — igata R1 commissioning (R-phase activation precedent)\n- ADR-2605252200 — watatsumi civilian submersible R0 (YouTube methodology adoption + structural exclusion pattern)\n- ADR-2605261115 — makura foam pillow R0 (§2(c) anti-surveillance applied to consumer good precedent; G14 + N9 no-electronics → tsutae G6 with-electronics translation)\n- ADR-2605252400 — kanayama circular metallurgy R0 (EOL Al recycling downstream consumer)\n- ADR-2605250500 — yakushi pharmaceutical master charter (14 gates + 10 non-goals canonical Tier-B R0 pattern)\n- ADR-2605242500 — baien ternary silicon + tsukuru fab charter (silicon Wave 1 SoC upstream supplier)\n- ADR-2605242515 — iwakura ternary inference ASIC (R2+ tsutae SoC integration target)\n- ADR-2605242600 — baien federated training via ameno WebGPU R0 (tsutae device = baien federated participant)\n- ADR-2605260200 — mitate R1 self-care advisory PWA (tsutae device = mitate PWA target platform)\n- ADR-2605261045 — manabi education R0 (G3 anti-addiction UX precedent; tsutae G8 OS-level translation)\n- ADR-2605192100 — etzhayyim Mission Charter (§1.3 communication infrastructure + §1.13 Wellbecoming)\n- ADR-2605192200 — Charter Compliance Rider v2.0 (§2(b) IP locking + §2(c) surveillance + §2(d) addiction + §2(e) repair / anti-gatekeeping)\n- ADR-2605191524 — transparent force swarm broadcast witness quorum (G4 invariant)\n- ADR-2605181100 — MST encrypted records + Signal key-wrap (G11 + G14 device DID + encrypted-record-capable invariant)\n- ADR-2605201400 — kuni-umi planetary-infra fleet (robotics class lineage)\n- YouTube `J4GoOScUO5k` — \"How Samsung Produces Millions of Expensive Smartphones Inside Massive Factories\" (Samsung Galaxy flagship factory build documentary; methodology source; manufacturing methodology adopted; surveillance / addiction / IP locking / closed bootloader / mass production at any cost rejected per §2(b) + §2(c) + §2(d) + §2(e))\n", :adr/path "90-docs/adr/2605261300-tsutae-handheld-communication-tier-b-actor-r0.edn", :adr/source-repo "root", :adr/topic "tsutae/smartphone/handheld", :adr/last_verified "2026-05-26T00:00:00Z", :adr/date "2026-05-26T00:00:00Z", :adr/authoritative true, :adr/related ["adr-2605242500-baien-ternary-silicon-and-tsukuru-fab-charter" "adr-2605242515-iwakura-ternary-inference-asic" "adr-2605252200-watatsumi-civilian-submersible-r0" "adr-2605261115-makura-foam-pillow-tier-b-actor-r0" "adr-2605261115-igata-megacasting-tier-b-actor-r0" "adr-2605192100-etzhayyim-mission-charter" "adr-2605192200-etzhayyim-ip-free-release-charter-rider"]}]
